metadata.Note:
- The course emphasizes a semester-long MLOps capstone project, where students progressively design, implement, deploy, and monitor a real-world machine learning system following industry-standard MLOps practices. The project is developed through four milestone reports aligned with the MLOps lifecycle.
- The final mark is determined by summing the weighted scores of: Progress Test 1 (10%), Report 1 – Project Scoping & Lifecycle Design (10%), Report 2 – Data Pipeline & Reproducibility Setup (10%), Report 3 – Automated Pipeline & Model Testing (30%), Report 4 – Model Serving & Active Monitoring (10%), and Final Exam (30%).
- The four project reports progressively evaluate students' ability to:
- define and scope an ML problem and design its lifecycle;
- build reproducible data pipelines with version control and experiment tracking;
- implement automated ML pipelines with testing and continuous integration;
- deploy, monitor, and maintain production-ready ML services using modern MLOps tools.
- The final examination is a computer-based multiple-choice examination covering the theoretical and practical foundations of MLOps across the entire course, including ML lifecycle management, data engineering, reproducibility, pipeline automation, deployment, CI/CD, monitoring, and operational excellence.
- Completion Criteria: every assessment component > 0 AND Final Exam Score ≥ 4.0 AND Final Result ≥ 5.0.
